  <div class="tip">
    <strong>Quick Tips:</strong><br>
    ✅ Swap black for deep brown or olive<br>
    ✅ Swap white for cream or warm beige<br>
    ✅ Choose soft/muted tones over bright or icy colors<br>
    ✅ Matte and textured materials flatter your tone<br>
    ✅ Earthy palettes are your best friend!
  </div>

  <div class="tip">
    <strong>Outfit Planning Guidelines:</strong><br>
    🎨 Aim for this color distribution in outfits:<br>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>60%</strong> – Best Neutrals (e.g., camel pants, cream tops)</li>
      <li><strong>30%</strong> – Best Colors (e.g., dusty rose blouse, moss green dress)</li>
      <li><strong>10%</strong> – Accent Colors (e.g., goldenrod scarf, soft peach bag)</li>
    </ul>
    👗 For balance, let one piece shine — if you wear a bold muted teal coat, keep the rest neutral.<br>
    🧣 Use accessories to introduce accent colors without overwhelming your palette.<br>
    👞 Shoes and bags look great in warm neutrals like taupe, olive, or warm gray.
  </div>
